ing  demand for more powerful submarines  nuclear-powered subs can remain  submerged for longer amounts of time are  larger and are also more expensive but  when it comes to submerged propulsion  speed underwater nuclear power is simply  the better option the value of the  nuclear subs seems to have overweight  the value of the diesel ones and  australia has announced that their deal  with france is over as they put in a new  order with the united states for at  least eight nuclear-powered  hunter-killer submarines as part of  their new security pact  across the world are putting their  attention towards the indo-pacific a  pretty large place it's home to sixty  percent of the world's population  produces sixty percent of the global gdp  and it's also the second largest  destination for exports from the eu for  member states like france a country with  more than a million citizens in the area  as well as stationed troops their  objectives have been made clear france  wants to be a stabilizing force promote  the values of freedom in the rule of law  and help solve certain geopolitical  challenges  for the eu specifically by pivoting off  of individual member states own goals as  well as being primarily led by france  the eu has announced that they will  focus on reinforcing cooperation promote  a rules-based international order keep  open markets and ensure stable trading  environment however unfortunately for  them on the same day that the eu was set  to make their official announcement for  their indo-pacific strategy auckus was  also announced and that means that the  three countries that were already  notorious for being excessively loud  when it's not socially acceptable  decided to announce their own private  clubhouse in the indo-pacific region  overshadowing the eu's announcement and  forcing europe to reconsider their  overall strategy  mcclellan has already begun signaling  for a larger push in european  sovereignty saying things like europeans  must stop b